      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Convex geometry playground\n\nTOP (BLUE) - hull and concavity: an L-shape is synthesized from two filled rectangles, its contour is bridged to a point array ('CV Contour To Points') and fed to cv2.convexHull twice - once for the hull POINTS (green outline via 'CV Points To Contour'), once for the hull INDICES that cv2.convexityDefects needs (its depth column / 256 = how deep the notch cuts, ~85 px here). 'CV Filter Contours' reads the matching solidity ratio (~0.78).\n\nMIDDLE (YELLOW) - point-in-polygon: cv2.pointPolygonTest returns the SIGNED distance to the L-shape's edge (positive inside, negative outside).\n\nBOTTOM (RED) - polygon IoU: two overlapping quads authored with 'CV Points' go through the embedded 'Polygon IoU (convex)' subgraph (cv2.intersectConvexConvex + contourArea + MathExpression). Expected IoU here: 4800 / 40000 = 0.12. Disjoint quads give 0.0, not an error.\n\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
